ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  A fleet of ships carried the banner of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0) into the Sea province of the Mirkwood Sea, ruled by Circe.  Alain (#33)
's forces conquered the Mirkwood Sea without any major engagements.  Alain 
leads approximately 1 Phalanx, 1 Legion, 4 Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  Silvermist was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 71st Legion in 
Silvermist and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 154th Legion in 
Silvermist and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 233rd Chariots in 
Silvermist and destroyed them.  Circe's forces fought in a battle in Katanga,
but a foreign general commanded it.  The battle is in the General 
Intelligence Report.

  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
invaded Balmwood, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Circe and made up 
of extensive Forests.  Uga-Buga Makumb's armies took possession of Balmwood 
practically uncontested.  Uga-Buga Makumb leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 4 
Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  Circe's forces fought in a battle in Katanga, but a foreign general 
commanded it.  The battle is in the General Intelligence Report.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
entered Silvermist, hoping to subjugate that province owned by Circe and 
made up of extensive Mountains.  Uga-Buga Makumb's forces encountered little 
opposition in Silvermist and Uga-Buga Makumb there established our rule.  
Uga-Buga Makumb leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 4 Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Circe for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Circe's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Circe was left with 23 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Gridley, Squire to Jamielle
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Jamielle was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it came 
to pass that Jamielle met her tragic end.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Jamielle


From: Gridley, Squire to Philo
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Philo was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it came to 
pass that Philo met his unseemly end.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Philo


From: Tattoo, Squire to Reynald
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Arnulf (#19) encountered Reynald.  Chanting his syllables of magic with 
trained precision, Arnulf let fly a Hand Of Death spell and began making 
squeezing motions with his hands.  Reynald turned to flee from Arnulf, but 
found that his retreat route had been magically blocked by a curtain of 
shimmering force.
  Reynald moved to bow range.  Arnulf brought his hands together and yanked 
them apart in a ripping motion, provoking a squeal from Reynald and scored 3 
damage points on him.  Arnulf curled his phantasmal hand around Reynald's 
heart and squeezed it viciously and inflicted 3 damage points.
  Reynald charged into melee range.  He then thrust at Arnulf and would have 
struck him if Arnulf hadn't sidestepped just then.  Arnulf brought his hands 
together and yanked them apart in a ripping gesture, provoking a squeal from 
Reynald and scorched him with 3 damage points.  Reynald flamboyantly flipped 
over Arnulf and swang at him and damaged him, inflicting 4 damage points.  
His spell was disrupted by the event.  Arnulf circled left and assailed 
Reynald and scored on him, doing 1 points of damage.  Reynald was fatally 
wounded.  Thus did Reynald die, a brave end by any standard.  Arnulf took 
the pack Reynald had borne.  Arnulf found a treasure of 1 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Reynald


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Alexius
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Alexius was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  Thus did 
Alexius die, a brave end by any standard.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alexius


