GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT


Kingdom of Prometeo (#5):
  From Circe:  In fall, a host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Jungle province of Katanga, 
ruled by Circe.  Pascal (#78) commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders 
were led by Prometeo (#5).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Katanga (0404):

 283rd/VS  284th/AS  282nd/VS 
  Legion   Chariots   Legion  
 |||01|||  |||01|||  |||01||| 
------------------------------
 |||05|||  |||05|||  |||05||| 
 231st/V    24th/A   262nd/A  
  Legion   Hvy Cav   Hvy Cav  
                              
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Pascal (#78) led his armies into the fray.  Prometeo (#5) commanded a host 
of loyal soldiers.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The two armies raced for the high ground, and Pascal 
(#78) obtained an advantage by getting there before the enemy.  On the other 
hand in spite of his industrious planning, Pascal was tactically 
outmaneuvered and soon realized that this affair would be an uphill battle.
  Prometeo (#5) started with an inspiring speech to his army, which 
bolstered their morale.
  Out on the right wing, the Veteran 283rd Legion were arrayed against the 
Veteran 231st Legion, who were stiffened by a hardened band of mercenaries 
of the Mercenaries Guild, who exhorted them to a fanatical charge by example 
of their experienced elan.  In this match, a rumor was circulated among the 
231st Legion that they would be given medals if they won the battle, which 
bestowed upon the 231st Legion the psychological advantage.  The 283rd 
Legion fought the 231st Legion and fought courageously, but was steadily 
pushed back.
  In the interior lines, the 284th Skeletal Chariots were arrayed against 
the 24th Heavy Cavalry.  The squadrons of the 24th Heavy Cavalry experienced 
a tough challenge against the easily defensible Chariots.  In this area, the 
284th Skeletal Chariots were slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of 
ground and they joined the fight at a tiny disadvantage.  It seemed that the 
24th Heavy Cavalry might win the battle.
  Then the tide of battle turned.  A few of the soldiers of the 24th 
Heavy Cavalry got lost in a patch of fog, which whittled down their numbers 
slightly.  The 284th Skeletal Chariots battled with the 24th Heavy Cavalry 
and were bent back by their attack.
  On the left flank, the Veteran 282nd Skeletal Legion faced the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry.  The Heavy Cavalry troops bore down on the 282nd Skeletal 
Legion and shook them with the terrible impact.  In this sector, many men of 
the 262nd Heavy Cavalry were recovering from the flu, weakening their 
fighting spirit significantly.  The 282nd Skeletal Legion fought the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry and managed to make some slow progress.
  The host of Prometeo crushed the army of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s fighting 
spirit with one last push.  The 231st Legion destroyed the 283rd Legion.  
Pascal (#78)'s armies were beaten and pushed out of Katanga.  Pascal set out 
for the safety of Chaco with his motley army.

  From Circe:  In early winter, a host of savage warriors carried the banner 
of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Jungle province of Katanga,
held by Circe.  Tlazolteotl (#88) was in command of the attacking armies.  
The defending forces were commanded by Prometeo (#5).  The armies were drawn 
up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Katanga (0404):

   75th     256th     106th   
 Dragons   Dragons   Dragons  
 |||00|||  |||00|||  |||00||| 
                              
 222nd/C   223rd/C   139th/C  
 Phalanx   Phalanx   Phalanx  
 |||00|||  |||00|||  |||00||| 
------------------------------
 |||05|||  |||05|||  |||05||| 
 262nd/V    24th/A   231st/V  
 Hvy Cav   Hvy Cav    Legion  
                              
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with her warriors was Tlazolteotl (#88).  Prometeo 
(#5) stood ready at the head of his thousands.
  Tlazolteotl (#88) strode forward and challenged Prometeo (#5) to honorable 
combat.  Prometeo accepted the challenge to honorable combat.  And so it 
came to pass that Prometeo met his tragic end.  The forces commanded by 
Prometeo were disheartened by his demise, yet still they pressed ahead with 
some hope of victory.  As luck would have it, Tlazolteotl (#88)'s formations 
were partially concealed by a sudden mist, giving them a small edge.  Also, 
Tlazolteotl maneuvered her forces against the acting commander with 
excellent tactical judgement and enjoyed an important tactical advantage.
  Prometeo (#5) started with an inspiring speech to his army, raising their 
courage.
  On the right flank, the Crack 222nd Phalanx were arrayed against the 
Veteran 262nd Heavy Cavalry.  The 75th Dragons swooped down on the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry and attacked without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl (#88) switched the 75th Dragons to the fore, angling for a 
better match-up.  The poor horses of the 262nd Heavy Cavalry were spooked by 
the Beasts they beheld.  The 75th Dragons battled with the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry and squashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  Within the interior lines, the Crack 223rd Phalanx were arrayed against 
the 24th Heavy Cavalry.  The 256th Dragons swooped down on the 24th 
Heavy Cavalry and attacked without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 256th Dragons to the front line, as a strategem 
for a superior match-up.  The nervous horses of the 24th Heavy Cavalry were 
frightened by the Beasts they were faced with.  The 256th Dragons fought 
with the 24th Heavy Cavalry and mowed them down like weeds.
  On the left outside wing, the Crack 139th Phalanx faced the Veteran 231st 
Legion.  The clumsy mass of the 139th Phalanx was tested by the maneuverable 
Legionnaires.  The 106th Dragons soared over the 231st Legion and attacked 
without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 106th Dragons to the fore, as a strategem for a 
superior nemesis effect.  On this field, the 106th Dragons immediately 
turned in flight when they contacted their enemy.  But it soon became clear 
that the retreat was a feigned one, a trick to lure their enemy into 
overextending himself.  The 106th Dragons fought with the 231st Legion and 
advanced at will.
  The forces of Tlazolteotl broke through the lines of their opposition and 
were victorious.  The 75th Dragons destroyed the 262nd Heavy Cavalry.  The 
256th Dragons annihilated the 24th Heavy Cavalry.  The 106th Dragons 
demolished the 231st Legion.  Tlazolteotl's host concluded the campaign 
victoriously and conquered the province of Katanga.  Its forces completely 
dispersed, the acting commander escaped frightened and alone to Cantia.


END MOVES REPORT

